@host = http://localhost:5080

### A malformed address is refused, field by field, without anything throwing.
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "street": "", "city": "Utrecht", "postalCode": "nope", "lines": [] }

### A good address, a line with no SKU. 422 before an order exists in the database at all: the handler
### builds the aggregate, asks it what that broke, and refuses. The order answered for its line, and
### nothing was added to a context, queried or saved to find that out.
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "street": "Oudegracht 1",
  "city": "Utrecht",
  "postalCode": "3511 AA",
  "lines": [{ "sku": "   ", "quantity": 1 }]
}

### A good one. Note the ORD_ prefix on the id that comes back.
# @name placed
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "street": "Oudegracht 1",
  "city": "Utrecht",
  "postalCode": "3511 AA",
  "lines": [{ "sku": "COFFEE-1KG", "quantity": 2 }]
}

### A second later, Shipping has booked against it. It never saw an Order.
GET {{host}}/shipments

### Amending the order bumps Version. Two of these at once gives one caller a 409.
POST {{host}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.id}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "MUG", "quantity": 1 }

### The same on an order that is already in the database: 422, and the code is the child entity's own.
### The handler asked the order, the order asked its lines, and the body names the line that is at
### fault, because the violation carries its id. The save would have stopped it either way.
POST {{host}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.id}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "   ", "quantity": 1 }

### The same SKU twice: 422 again, but the code is CheckInvariants, because that rule stayed a seam.
### Only the order can see both lines, which is why the rule is the root's rather than the line's, and
### it is the same one call that found the line's rule above. The boundary answers for both.
POST {{host}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.id}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "MUG", "quantity": 1 }

### The id parses with or without its prefix.
GET {{host}}/orders/{{placed.response.body.id}}
